        "content": "## NVDA News, from 2026-04-28 to 2026-05-05:\n\n### Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang says company now has zero market share in China (source: Yahoo Finance)\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang says the company's market share in China has fallen to zero.\nLink: https://finance.yahoo.com/sectors/technology/article/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-says-company-now-has-zero-market-share-in-china-150805330.html\n\n### The Utility Stock That's Actually Exciting (source: Motley Fool)\nOklo is trying to flip the traditional utility model on its head.\nLink: https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/05/04/the-utility-stock-thats-actually-exciting/\n\n### Marvell Stock: A 16% Yield Trade With A 46% Margin of Safety (source: Trefis)\nMarvell (MRVL) has been one of the quieter names in semiconductors through the AI boom, until recently. A $2 billion strategic investment from Nvidia, advanced chip co-development talks with Alphabet, and multiple confirmed cloud-provider design wins have sent the stock up 50% in the last month alone. See why Marvell stock moved.\nLink: https://www.trefis.com/articles/598200/marvell-stock-a-16-yield-trade-with-a-46-margin-of-safety/2026-05-04\n\n### Big Tech pulled into growing AI capacity concerns (source: GuruFocus.com)\nCapacity concerns push government to widen partners\nLink: https://finance.yahoo.com/sectors/technology/articles/big-tech-pulled-growing-ai-165832927.html\n\n### AI Chipmaker Cerebras Targets Raising Up To $4 billion in IPO (source: MT Newswires)\nCerebras Systems plans to kick off the roadshow for its proposed initial public offering as the arti\nLink: https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ai-chipmaker-cerebras-targets-raising-165027661.html\n\n### SIVR Beats SLV. Here Is Why. (source: Motley Fool)\nThis smaller silver ETF is a better long-term investment than the market leader.\nLink: https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/05/04/sivr-beats-slv-here-is-why/\n\n### Cerebras Systems seeks up to $26.6B valuation in US IPO (source: Proactive)\nCerebras Systems is targeting a valuation of as much as $26.62 billion in its planned U.S. initial public offering, according to its prospectus filings. The semiconductor company, which is positioning itself as a rival to Nvidia in AI hardware, is looking to sell 28 million shares of its...\nLink: https://www.proactiveinvestors.com/companies/news/1091666/cerebras-systems-seeks-up-to-26-6b-valuation-in-us-ipo-1091666.html\n\n### Did Anthropic Suck the Air From Palantir’s Commercial Contract Tailwinds? (source: 24/7 Wall St.)\nPalantir Technologies (NASDAQ: PLTR) reports Q1 2026 results after the close today. Management guided at least 115% U.S. commercial growth for the year just as Anthropic’s enterprise AI push reshaped software buying. I’ll be watching whether commercial momentum held. Commercial Acceleration Meets a New Competitor Last quarter Palantir delivered $1.41B in revenue, up 70% YoY, ... Did Anthropic Suck the Air From Palantir’s Commercial Contract Tailwinds?\nLink: https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/05/04/did-anthropic-suck-the-air-from-palantirs-commercial-contract-tailwinds/\n\n### AMD Sinks 6% Despite a Holding Pattern in Intel and NVIDIA: The Selective AI Chip Trade Is Here (source: 24/7 Wall St.)\nShares of Advanced Micro Devices (NASDAQ:AMD) are sinking 6% in midday trading Monday, changing hands near $340 after closing Friday at $360.54. The selloff stands out because AMD’s peers are barely moving. Intel (NASDAQ:INTC) stock is down 2% and NVIDIA (NASDAQ:NVDA) stock is off just 1%. After months of correlated moves higher, the artificial intelligence ... AMD Sinks 6% Despite a Holding Pattern in Intel and NVIDIA: The Selective AI Chip Trade Is Here\nLink: https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/05/04/amd-sinks-6-despite-a-holding-pattern-in-intel-and-nvidia-the-selective-ai-chip-trade-is-here/\n\n### Wall Street Sees 21% Upside for Rivian Despite R2 Pricing Disappointment (source: 24/7 Wall St.)\nRivian (NASDAQ:RIVN) currently trades around $15, while Wall Street’s average price target sits at $18.16. That means analysts see roughly 21% upside for the stock today. Rivian designs and builds premium electric trucks, SUVs, and commercial vans, and is now betting its future on the R2 platform, a next-generation, lower-cost SUV designed for the mass market. ... Wall Street Sees 21% Upside for Rivian Despite R2 Pricing Disappointment\nLink: https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/05/04/wall-street-sees-21-upside-for-rivian-despite-r2-pricing-disappointment/\n\n### Jim Cramer Just Won’t Give Up on NVIDIA (NVDA) (source: Insider Monkey)\nWe recently published Jim Cramer Commented On Big Market Confusion & Discussed These 20 Stocks. NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) is one of the stocks discussed by Jim Cramer. NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) is one of Jim Cramer’s favorite stocks. Throughout 2025 and 2026, the CNBC TV host has defended the firm during periods of weak share price […]\nLink: https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/jim-cramer-just-won-t-162058779.html\n\n### Intel's Stock Hits a New All-Time High: Is It Still a Buy? (source: Motley Fool)\nShares of the tech giant are up around 170% this year.\nLink: https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/05/04/intels-stock-hits-a-new-all-time-high-is-it-still/\n\n### History Says Nvidia's 2026 Run Is Just Getting Started (source: Motley Fool)\nThe chipmaker's stock is still trading at valuations below its average from the past few years.\nLink: https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/05/04/history-says-nvidias-2026-run-is-just-getting-star/\n\n### NVIDIA Broadens AI Reach Into Quantum Nuclear Power And Healthcare Robotics (source: Simply Wall St.)\nNVIDIA (NasdaqGS:NVDA) has released open-source Ising AI models that link its GPU platforms with quantum-inspired computing. The company is working with nuclear energy partners, including Oklo and Los Alamos, on AI infrastructure for reactor design and operations. NVIDIA is expanding in healthcare robotics through partners such as Proximie. The company is backing AI-first cloud providers like Nebius and extending its AI infrastructure with partners including Vultr, Netris and...\nLink: https://finance.yahoo.com/sectors/technology/articles/nvidia-broadens-ai-reach-quantum-161150820.html\n\n### Despite Soaring 46%, ConocoPhillips Is a Hold as Price Target Trails (source: 24/7 Wall St.)\nOur ConocoPhillips (NYSE:COP) call comes on the heels of a mixed Q1 2026 earnings report, where adjusted earnings beat but revenue missed amid softer realized prices. Below is the verdict, the math, and the scenarios that could move it. The 24/7 Wall St. Price Target for ConocoPhillips Our 24/7 Wall St. price target for ConocoPhillips ... Despite Soaring 46%, ConocoPhillips Is a Hold as Price Target Trails\nLink: https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/05/04/despite-soaring-46-conocophillips-is-a-hold-as-price-target-trails/\n\n### Is Microsoft a Buy as Cloud Revenue Continues to Soar? (source: Motley Fool)\nMicrosoft's stock has been running in place for the past two years.\nLink: https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/05/04/is-microsoft-a-buy-as-cloud-revenue-continues-to/\n\n### Gen Digital to Report Q4 Earnings: What's in Store for the Stock? (source: Zacks)\nGEN heads into Q4 results with strong growth forecasts, AI-driven product momentum and rising cybersecurity demand, but margin pressure and weak sentiment loom.\nLink: https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/gen-digital-report-q4-earnings-154500551.html\n\n### Broadcom, Google And Caterpillar Lead AI Charge On Must-See List (source: Investor's Business Daily)\nBroadcom stock teases a buy zone as fellow IBD Leaderboard members Google and Caterpillar climb out of buy range.\nLink: https://www.investors.com/research/how-to-find-the-best-stocks-to-buy/broadcom-stock-google-caterpillar-leaderboard-ai-stocks/?src=A00220&yptr=yahoo\n\n### Coinbase Has 26% Upside to Price Targets After 57% Selloff (source: 24/7 Wall St.)\nCoinbase (NASDAQ:COIN)