        "content": "# Comprehensive Fundamental Analysis Report: NVIDIA Corporation (NVDA)\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nNVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA) is a global technology company and one of the most influential players in the semiconductor industry. The company has experienced remarkable growth driven by explosive demand for AI/ML computing infrastructure, data center solutions, and GPU-based products. This report provides a detailed analysis of NVIDIA's fundamental financial health, balance sheet strength, cash flow generation, and income statement performance to inform trading decisions.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Company Profile\n\n| Attribute | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Company Name** | NVIDIA Corporation |\n| **Ticker** | NVDA |\n| **Sector** | Technology |\n| **Industry** | Semiconductors |\n| **Market Cap** | ~$4.80 trillion |\n| **50-Day Avg Price** | $187.15 |\n| **200-Day Avg Price** | $183.86 |\n| **52-Week Range** | $110.82 – $216.83 |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key Valuation Metrics\n\n| Metric | Value | Analysis |\n|--------|-------|----------|\n| **PE Ratio (TTM)** | 40.34 | Premium valuation reflecting growth expectations |\n| **Forward PE** | 17.59 | Significant decline expected as earnings grow into multiple |\n| **PEG Ratio** | 0.63 | Below 1.0 suggests reasonable valuation relative to growth |\n| **Price-to-Book** | 30.54 | High multiple, typical for tech leaders with strong ROI |\n| **EPS (TTM)** | $4.90 | Trailing twelve-month earnings per share |\n| **Forward EPS** | $11.24 | Analysts expect more than 100% earnings growth |\n| **Dividend Yield** | 0.02% | Minimal yield; growth-oriented investor focus |\n| **Beta** | 2.244 | High volatility — more sensitive to market swings |\n\n**Insight:** NVIDIA trades at a premium valuation (40x PE), but the forward PE of 17.6x implies strong earnings acceleration anticipated over the next 12 months. The PEG ratio of 0.63 suggests the stock is reasonably priced relative to projected growth.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Financial Performance (TTM)\n\n| Metric (TTM) | Value | % of Revenue |\n|--------------|-------|--------------|\n| **Revenue** | $215.9B | 100% |\n| **Gross Profit** | $153.5B | 71.1% |\n| **EBITDA** | $133.2B | 61.7% |\n| **Net Income** | $120.1B | 55.6% |\n| **Profit Margin** | 55.6% | — |\n| **Operating Margin** | 65.0% | — |\n\n**Insight:** NVIDIA demonstrates exceptional profitability with a 55.6% net profit margin and 65% operating margin — among the highest in the semiconductor sector. The gross margin of 71% reflects strong pricing power and product differentiation in high-demand AI chips.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Return Metrics & Efficiency\n\n| Metric | Value | Assessment |\n|--------|-------|-------------|\n| **Return on Equity (ROE)** | 101.5% | Exceptional — generating >$1 of profit per $1 of equity |\n| **Return on Assets (ROA)** | 51.2% | Very high asset efficiency |\n| **Free Cash Flow (TTM)** | $58.1B | Strong cash generation |\n| **Debt to Equity** | 7.26 | Moderate leverage; manageable given cash flows |\n\n**Insight:** ROE exceeding 100% is outstanding and signals highly efficient use of shareholder capital. The company generates substantial free cash flow relative to market cap, supporting ongoing growth investments and potential share repurchases.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Balance Sheet Analysis (Q1 FY2026 — As of January 31, 2026)\n\n### Key Balance Sheet Items\n\n| Item | Q1 2026 | Q4 2025 | Q3 2025 | Q2 2025 | Q1 2025 |\n|------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n| **Total Assets** | $206.8B | $161.1B | $140.7B | $125.3B | $111.6B |\n| **Total Equity** | $157.3B | $118.9B | $100.1B | $83.8B | $79.3B |\n| **Total Debt** | $11.04B | $10.48B | $10.60B | $10.29B | $9.98B |\n| **Working Capital** | $93.4B | $90.4B | $78.0B | $63.4B | $62.1B |\n| **Current Ratio** | 3.905 | — | — | — | — |\n| **Cash & Equivalents** | $10.6B | $11.5B | $11.6B | $15.2B | $8.6B |\n| **Inventory** | $21.4B | $19.8B | $15.0B | $11.3B | $10.1B |\n| **Receivables** | $38.5B | $33.4B | $27.8B | $22.1B | $23.1B |\n\n### Capital Structure\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Book Value per Share** | $6.47 |\n| **Tangible Book Value** | $133.2B |\n| **Goodwill & Intangibles** | $24.1B |\n| **Net PPE** | $13.3B |\n\n**Insight:** \n- **Strong liquidity:** Current ratio of 3.9x indicates excellent short-term liquidity.\n- **Growing asset base:** Total assets have grown from $111.6B to $206.8B YoY, reflecting aggressive capacity expansion.\n- **Low leverage:** Debt-to-equity of 7.26 is moderate; the company has significant cash generation capacity to service debt.\n- **Inventory build:** Inventory has more than doubled from $10.1B to $21.4B over the past year, indicating preparation for higher demand.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Quarterly Income Statement (Q1 FY2026 — Ended January 31, 2026)\n\n| Line Item | Q1 FY2026 | Q4 FY2025 | Q3 FY2025 | Q2 FY2025 | Q1 FY2025 |\n|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|\n| **Revenue** | $68.13B | $57.01B | $46.74B | $44.06B | $39.33B |\n| **Cost of Revenue** | $17.03B | $15.16B | $12.89B | $17.39B | $10.61B |\n| **Gross Profit** | $51.09B | $41.85B | $33.85B | $26.67B | $28.72B |\n| **Operating Expenses** | $6.79B | $5.84B | $5.41B | $5.03B | $4.69B |\n| **R&D** | $5.51B | $4.71B | $4.29B | $3.99B | $3.71B |\n| **SG&A** | $1.28B | $1.13B | $1.12B | $1.04B | $0.98B |\n| **Operating Income** | $44.30B | $36.01B | $28.44B | $21.64B | $24.03B |\n| **Net Income** | $42.96B | $31.91B | $26.42B | $18.78B | $22.09B |\n| **Diluted EPS** | $1.76 | $1.30 | $1.08 | $0.76 | $0.89 |\n\n**Quarter-over-Quarter Analysis:**\n- **Revenue growth:** Q1 FY2026 revenue of $68.13B represents a 19.5% sequential increase from Q4 FY2025 ($57.01B) and a 73% YoY increase from Q1 FY2025 ($39.33B).\n- **Margin expansion:** Gross margin improved to 75.0% (51.09/68.13), up from 73.4% in Q4 FY2025.\n- **Net income surge:** Q1 net income of $42.96B grew 34.6% YoY, demonstrating operating leverage.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Cash Flow Analysis (Q1 FY2026)\n\n| Line Item | Q1 FY2026 | Q4 FY2025 | Q3 FY2025 | Q2 FY2025 | Q1 FY2025 |\n|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|\n| **Operating Cash Flow** | $36.19B | $23.75B | $15.37B | $27.41B | $16.63B |\n| **Capital Expenditures** | ($1.28B) | ($1.64B) | ($1.90B) | ($1.23B) | ($1.08B) |\n| **Free Cash Flow** | $34.90B | $22.12B | $13.47B | $26.19B | $15.55B |\n| **Free Cash Flow (TTM)** | $58.13B | — | — | — | — |\n\n### Cash Flow Trends\n\n| Metric | Observation |\n|--------|--------------|\n| **Operating Cash Flow** | Very strong, consistently positive; Q1 FY2026 at $36.2B |\n| **Capex** | Relatively modest at $1.3B, suggesting efficient capital deployment |\n| **Free Cash Flow Margin** | >50% of revenue — exceptional cash conversion |\n| **Share Repurchases** | $3.82B in Q1 FY2026; total $44B+ over trailing 12 months |\n| **Dividends** | Minimal ~$242M per quarter |\n\n**Insight:** NVIDIA converts a majority of revenue into free cash flow, providing significant financial flexibility for reinvestment, acquisitions, and shareholder returns. Capex remains modest relative to operating cash flow, indicating high incremental returns on capital.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Segment & Product Outlook (Qualitative)\n\nWhile detailed segment data is not provided in the API, key growth drivers based on recent earnings and industry trends include:\n\n1. **Data Center (AI/GPU Computing):** The primary growth driver — NVIDIA's A100, H100, and upcoming Blackwell GPUs power major cloud providers and AI startups. Revenue likely exceeds $45B+ annually in data center.\n2. **Gaming:** Steady demand for RTX GPUs and game console SoCs.\n3. **Automotive:** Growth in autonomous driving and AI enter car solutions.\n4. **Networking & Ethernet:** Spectrum AI switches and DPU accelerators expanding TAM.\n5. **Metaverse / Omniverse:** Enterprise software opportunities.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Key Risks & Considerations\n\n| Risk | Impact |\n|------|--------|\n| **High valuation (40x PE)** | Vulnerable to corrections if growth slows or guidance cuts |\n| **Concentration risk** | Heavy reliance on hyperscaler/capex spend; any macro slowdown in AI spending could impact results |\n| **Competitive pressure** | AMD, Intel, custom ASICs, and cloud-native chips from Google/Amazon |\n| **Supply chain constraints** | TSMC capacity allocation remains critical |\n| **High beta (2.24)** | Elevated volatility — amplified downside in market sell-offs |\n| **Regulatory risk** | Export restrictions to China continue to impact revenue potential |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Analyst & Trading Summary\n\n### Valuation Summary Table\n\n| Metric | Current | Forward (12M) |\n|--------|---------|---------------|\n| **PE Ratio** | 40.3x | 17.6x |\n| **PEG Ratio** | 0.63 | — |\n| **Price / Book** | 30.5x | — |\n| **EPS (TTM)** | $4.90 | $11.24 (est.) |\n| **Free Cash Flow/Share** | ~$2.38 | — |\n\n### Key Strengths\n- ✅ Best-in-class profitability (55%+ net margin, 100%+ ROE)\n- ✅ Strong free cash flow generation (>50% of revenue)\n- ✅ Dominant position in AI GPU infrastructure\n- ✅ Clean balance sheet with low leverage\n- ✅ Secular tailwinds from AI demand\n\n### Concerns\n- ⚠️ Premium valuation leaves limited margin of safety\n- ⚠️ High beta / volatility risk\n- ⚠️ Heavy dependency on hyperscale capex cycles\n- ⚠️ Competitive landscape intensifying\n\n---\n\n## 11. Actionable Insights for Traders\n\n1. **Short-Term (1-3 months):** The stock is trading near all-time highs ($187 vs. 52-week high $217). Given the high beta, any negative sentiment or broader market correction could trigger a 10-15% pullback. Consider partial profit-taking if long position.\n\n2. **Medium-Term (3-12 months):** Forward PE of 17.6x is reasonable given ~130% YoY EPS growth expectations. If the company delivers on FY2026 guidance, the stock could appreciate toward $250+.\n\n3. **Fundamental Tailwind:** With data center revenue accelerating and new product cycles (Blackwell), fundamentals remain robust. The stock is priced for excellence but still may have upward room given AI supercycle tailwinds.\n\n4. **Dividends & Buybacks:** Minimal dividend yield (0.02%) but active share repurchases (~$44B TTM) provide indirect return of capital. Watch for continued buyback authorization.\n\n5. **Technical Levels:** \n   - Support: $175 (50-day MA), $165, $150 \n   - Resistance: $200, $216.83 (all-time high)\n\n---\n\n## Recommendation Summary\n\n| Aspect | Assessment |\n|--------|-------------|\n| **Fundamental Quality** | ★★★★★ (Exceptional) |\n| **Valuation** | ★★★★☆ (Premium but justified by growth) |\n| **Risk/Reward** | ★★★★☆ (Favorable, but high beta) |\n| **Overall** | **BUY** for long-term investors; caution on short-term overbought conditions |\n\n**FINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: BUY**\n\n*Note: This analysis is based on fundamental data as of Q1 FY2026 (ending January 31, 2026). Trading decisions should consider broader market conditions, upcoming earnings releases, and macroeconomic factors.*\n\n---\n\n## Appendix: Key Data Summary Table\n\n| Category | Metric | Value (TTM / Latest) |\n|----------|--------|---------------------|\n| **Market Data** | Market Cap | $4.80 Trillion |\n| | PE Ratio (TTM) | 40.34 |\n| | Forward PE | 17.59 |\n| | PEG Ratio | 0.63 |\n| | Price / Book | 30.54 |\n| | Beta | 2.24 |\n| **Profitability** | Revenue | $215.9 B |\n| | Gross Margin | 71.1% |\n| | Operating Margin | 65.0% |\n| | Net Margin | 55.6% |\n| | Net Income | $120.1 B |\n| | ROE | 101.5% |\n| | ROA | 51.2% |\n| **Cash Flow** | Free Cash Flow | $58.1 B |\n| | Operating CF | $36.2 B (Q1) |\n| **Balance Sheet** | Total Assets | $206.8 B |\n| | Total Equity | $157.3 B |\n| | Total Debt | $11.04 B |\n| | Current Ratio | 3.91 |\n| | Debt / Equity | 7.26 |\n| **Quarterly (Q1 FY2026)** | Revenue | $68.13 B |\n| | Net Income | $42.96 B |\n| | EPS (Diluted) | $1.76 |\n| | Gross Margin | 75.0% |\n\n---\n\n*Report generated on May 5, 2026. Data sourced from 